{
 "description": "Use before writing or fixing TikZ/LaTeX diagrams for render_diagram (format tikz): full-document wrapper, required libraries, LaTeX escaping, node-name restrictions, error meanings, worked examples, identifier rule.",
 "identifier": "Use the identifier as the node name and the display name as the text: `\\node[draw] (n0002) {engine};`. Node names may use letters, digits and `_` but NOT `.` (`public.orders` fails), so convert dots/slashes to `_` in the name and keep the real id in the label text. Never invent identifiers.",
